#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complex_plot3d

#% text
# `complex_plot3d(f, [z, z0, z1])` draws the modulus of f over the rectangle with corners z0 and z1 as a surface, coloured by the argument.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Heights are clipped above a robust range, so poles do not flatten the rest.

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG with SVG and PDF copies next to it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A pole:

#% cell
complex_plot3d(1/z, [z, -1 - im, 1 + im])
#% output
#= image("complex_plot3d.files/complex_plot3d-1.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A polynomial:

#% cell
complex_plot3d(z^3 - 1, [z, -1.5 - 1.5im, 1.5 + 1.5im])
#% output
#= image("complex_plot3d.files/complex_plot3d-2.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# From above:

#% cell
complex_plot3d(z^2, [z, -1 - im, 1 + im], view_point: above)
#% output
#= image("complex_plot3d.files/complex_plot3d-3.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `complex_plot`, `plot3d`
